  "Short_Summary": "A comprehensive guide to the UPSC Civil Services Examination structure, covering Prelims, Mains, and Personality Test stages.\r\nUnderstand the complete exam timeline, key stages, important milestones, and preparation roadmap for a well-structured UPSC journey.\r",
  "Full_Content": "<h2 class=\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-serif font-bold text-[#6C1D18] mt-8 text-left\" style=\"line-height: 1.03; margin-bottom: 12px;\"><strong>UPSC CIVIL SERVICES EXAMINATION</strong></h2><div class=\"overflow-x-auto my-8 rounded-xl border border-stone-300 shadow-sm\"><table class=\"w-full text-left border-collapse text-sm md:text-base\"><thead class=\"bg-[#6C1D18]/5 border-b border-stone-300 text-[#6C1D18] font-serif font-bold\"><tr><th class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-900 font-bold border-r border-stone-300 last:border-r-0\">&nbsp;</th><th class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-900 font-bold border-r border-stone-300 last:border-r-0\">&nbsp;</th></tr></thead><tbody class=\"divide-y divide-stone-200\"><tr><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">&nbsp;</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">&nbsp;</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"height: 12px;\"></div><h3 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-serif font-semibold text-[#6C1D18] mt-6 text-left\" style=\"line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>1.</strong>  <strong>The UPSC Examination Journey &amp; Timeline</strong></h3><p class=\"text-stone-800 text-base md:text-lg text-left\" style=\"line-height: 1.25; margin-bottom: 12px;\">The Civil Services Examination (CSE) operates on a highly structured, rigorous annual cycle. A single attempt spans nearly 15–16 months. The examination process progresses through three major successive phases as outlined in the official examination timeline:</p><div style=\"height: 12px;\"></div><div class=\"overflow-x-auto my-8 rounded-xl border border-stone-300 shadow-sm\"><table class=\"w-full text-left border-collapse text-sm md:text-base\"><thead class=\"bg-[#6C1D18]/5 border-b border-stone-300 text-[#6C1D18] font-serif font-bold\"><tr><th class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-900 font-bold border-r border-stone-300 last:border-r-0\"><strong>Year</strong></th><th class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-900 font-bold border-r border-stone-300 last:border-r-0\"><strong>Phase</strong></th><th class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-900 font-bold border-r border-stone-300 last:border-r-0\"><strong>Key Milestone Events &amp; Process</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody class=\"divide-y divide-stone-200\"><tr><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">Year 1</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">Jan–Jun</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">Notification &amp; Preliminary Examination (Objective screening)</td></tr><tr class=\"bg-stone-50/50 hover:bg-amber-50/30 transition-colors\"><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">Year 1</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">September</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">Mains Examination (Conventional written descriptive papers)</td></tr><tr class=\"bg-white hover:bg-amber-50/30 transition-colors\"><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">Year 2</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">Jan–Apr</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">Interview / Personality Test (Conversational Board Assessment)</td></tr><tr class=\"bg-stone-50/50 hover:bg-amber-50/30 transition-colors\"><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">Year 2</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">Apr–May</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">Final Result (Cumulative merit ranking and service allocation)</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"height: 12px;\"></div><div style=\"height: 12px;\"></div><h3 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-serif font-semibold text-[#6C1D18] mt-6 text-left\" style=\"line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>2.</strong>  <strong>Comprehensive Exam Structure &amp; Evaluation Scheme</strong></h3><p class=\"text-stone-800 text-base md:text-lg text-justify\" style=\"line-height: 1.25; margin-bottom: 12px;\">The evaluation is split into a multi-stage process. The Preliminary Examination acts as a screening test, and the Main Examination (comprising the Written Papers and the Personality Test) determines the final merit ranking. Below is the structured breakdown of the markings and structures for both stages:</p><p class=\"text-stone-800 text-base md:text-lg text-left\" style=\"line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 12px;\"><strong>I.</strong>  <strong>Preliminary Examination Structure</strong></p><div style=\"height: 12px;\"></div><div class=\"overflow-x-auto my-8 rounded-xl border border-stone-300 shadow-sm\"><table class=\"w-full text-left border-collapse text-sm md:text-base\"><thead class=\"bg-[#6C1D18]/5 border-b border-stone-300 text-[#6C1D18] font-serif font-bold\"><tr><th class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-900 font-bold border-r border-stone-300 last:border-r-0\"><strong>Paper</strong></th><th class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-900 font-bold border-r border-stone-300 last:border-r-0\"><strong>Subject / Areas Covered</strong></th><th class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-900 font-bold border-r border-stone-300 last:border-r-0\"><strong>Qs</strong></th><th class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-900 font-bold border-r border-stone-300 last:border-r-0\"><strong>Duration</strong></th><th class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-900 font-bold border-r border-stone-300 last:border-r-0\"><strong>Solve Time</strong></th><th class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-900 font-bold border-r border-stone-300 last:border-r-0\"><strong>Correct Ans</strong></th><th class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-900 font-bold border-r border-stone-300 last:border-r-0\"><strong>Wrong Ans Penalty</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody class=\"divide-y divide-stone-200\"><tr><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">Paper I</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">General Studies (History, Geography, Polity, Economy, Environment, General Science, Current Affairs)</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">100</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">2 Hours</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">1 min 12 Sec</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">+2 Marks</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">1/3rd of Max = 0.66</td></tr><tr class=\"bg-stone-50/50 hover:bg-amber-50/30 transition-colors\"><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">Paper II</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">CSAT (Qualifying in nature; requires minimum 33% score)</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">80</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">2 Hours</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">1 min 30 Sec</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">+2.5 Marks</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">1/3rd of Max = 0.83</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"height: 12px;\"></div><p class=\"text-stone-800 text-base md:text-lg text-center\" style=\"line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 12px;\"><strong>II.</strong>  <strong>Mains Examination &amp; Final Evaluation Marks Summary</strong></p><div style=\"height: 12px;\"></div><div class=\"overflow-x-auto my-8 rounded-xl border border-stone-300 shadow-sm\"><table class=\"w-full text-left border-collapse text-sm md:text-base\"><thead class=\"bg-[#6C1D18]/5 border-b border-stone-300 text-[#6C1D18] font-serif font-bold\"><tr><th class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-900 font-bold border-r border-stone-300 last:border-r-0\"><strong>Mains / Interview Stage Component</strong></th><th class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-900 font-bold border-r border-stone-300 last:border-r-0\"><strong>Subject / Paper Topic</strong></th><th class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-900 font-bold border-r border-stone-300 last:border-r-0\"><strong>Marks Evaluation Structure</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody class=\"divide-y divide-stone-200\"><tr><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">Compulsory Qualifying (Paper A)</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">Indian Language (Selected from the 8th Schedule)</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">300 Marks (Qualifying; 25% required)</td></tr><tr class=\"bg-stone-50/50 hover:bg-amber-50/30 transition-colors\"><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">Compulsory Qualifying (Paper B)</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">English Language (Précis, comprehension, essay, etc.)</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">300 Marks (Qualifying; 25% required)</td></tr><tr class=\"bg-white hover:bg-amber-50/30 transition-colors\"><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">Mains Paper I</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">Essay (Multiple topics; concise, orderly expression)</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">250 Marks (Counted for final merit)</td></tr><tr class=\"bg-stone-50/50 hover:bg-amber-50/30 transition-colors\"><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">Mains Paper II</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">General Studies–I (Indian Heritage, History, Geography, Society)</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">250 Marks (Counted for final merit)</td></tr><tr class=\"bg-white hover:bg-amber-50/30 transition-colors\"><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">Mains Paper III</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">General Studies–II (Governance, Constitution, Polity, Social Justice, IR)</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">250 Marks (Counted for final merit)</td></tr><tr class=\"bg-stone-50/50 hover:bg-amber-50/30 transition-colors\"><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">Mains Paper IV</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">General Studies–III (Tech, Economy, Bio-diversity, Environment, Security, DM)</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">250 Marks (Counted for final merit)</td></tr><tr class=\"bg-white hover:bg-amber-50/30 transition-colors\"><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">Mains Paper V</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">General Studies–IV (Ethics, Integrity, Aptitude)</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">250 Marks (Counted for final merit)</td></tr><tr class=\"bg-stone-50/50 hover:bg-amber-50/30 transition-colors\"><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">Mains Paper VI</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">Optional Subject – Paper I</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">250 Marks (Counted for final merit)</td></tr><tr class=\"bg-white hover:bg-amber-50/30 transition-colors\"><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">Mains Paper VII</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">Optional Subject – Paper II</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">250 Marks (Counted for final merit)</td></tr><tr class=\"bg-stone-50/50 hover:bg-amber-50/30 transition-colors\"><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">Personality Test (Interview)</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">Oral Board Interview assessing personal suitability &amp; calibre</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">275 Marks (Counted for final merit)</td></tr><tr class=\"bg-white hover:bg-amber-50/30 transition-colors\"><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\"><strong>Written Papers Total</strong></td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\"><strong>Sum of Papers I to VII (7 papers of 250 Marks each)</strong></td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\"><strong>1750 Marks</strong></td></tr><tr class=\"bg-stone-50/50 hover:bg-amber-50/30 transition-colors\"><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\"><strong>Personality Test Interview</strong></td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\"><strong>Board Interview Marks</strong></td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\"><strong>275 Marks</strong></td></tr><tr class=\"bg-white hover:bg-amber-50/30 transition-colors\"><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\"><strong>Grand Total Marks</strong></td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\"><strong>Aggregate Merit List Maximum Score</strong></td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\"><strong>2025</strong> <strong>Marks</strong></td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"height: 12px;\"></div><h3 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-serif font-semibold text-[#6C1D18] mt-6 text-left\" style=\"line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 4px;\"><strong>3.</strong>  <strong>Official Optional Subjects Roster</strong></h3><p class=\"text-stone-800 text-base md:text-lg text-left\" style=\"line-height: 1.25; margin-bottom: 12px;\">Candidates must select one optional subject from the list below. The optional subject consists of two written papers (Paper I and Paper II), each carrying 250 marks. Level of optional subjects is broadly of the honours degree level (higher than bachelors and lower than masters, except for Engineering, Medical Science, and Law which correspond to the bachelors' degree):</p><div style=\"height: 12px;\"></div><p class=\"text-stone-800 text-base md:text-lg text-left\" style=\"line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 2px;\"><strong>Academic Optional Subjects (25 Disciplines)</strong></p><div style=\"height: 12px;\"></div><div class=\"overflow-x-auto my-8 rounded-xl border border-stone-300 shadow-sm\"><table class=\"w-full text-left border-collapse text-sm md:text-base\"><thead class=\"bg-[#6C1D18]/5 border-b border-stone-300 text-[#6C1D18] font-serif font-bold\"><tr><th class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-900 font-bold border-r border-stone-300 last:border-r-0\"><strong>Group A</strong></th><th class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-900 font-bold border-r border-stone-300 last:border-r-0\"><strong>Group B</strong></th><th class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-900 font-bold border-r border-stone-300 last:border-r-0\"><strong>Group C</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody class=\"divide-y divide-stone-200\"><tr><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">1. Agriculture</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">10. Geography</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">18. Philosophy</td></tr><tr class=\"bg-stone-50/50 hover:bg-amber-50/30 transition-colors\"><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">2. Animal Husbandry &amp; Veterinary Science</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">11. Geology</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">19. Physics</td></tr><tr class=\"bg-white hover:bg-amber-50/30 transition-colors\"><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">3. Anthropology</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">12. History</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">20. Political Science &amp; International Relations (PSIR)</td></tr><tr class=\"bg-stone-50/50 hover:bg-amber-50/30 transition-colors\"><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">4. Botany</td><td class=\"py-3 px-4 text-stone-800 align-top border-r border-stone-200 last:border-r-0\">1